{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Righteousness</b> — it lifts up a nation and exalts it when it does it." "<b>And kindness</b> — which the nations do. It is accounted as a sin-offering." "Another interpretation: Righteousness lifts up a nation — Israel." "And the kindness of the nations is sin — it is, for it is for idol worship, and the witness is Nebuchadnezzar: \"and break off your sin by righteousness\" (Daniel 4:24) — and this is the correct one."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {3 "העד נבוכדנצר resolved as 'the witness is Nebuchadnezzar,' citing Daniel 4:24; לע\"ג expanded as לעבודת גילולים (idol worship)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:54.324243866Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}